course: dictionary
lesson: 4536
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. Hearing is the sense that lets you notice sounds with your ears. «Close your eyes and touch your nose: no sight, hearing, smell, taste or touch told you where your hand was.» Here hearing is one of your five senses, and it is a thing you have.
explain: Hearing can also be an action. Hear means to notice sounds, and hearing is its -ing form. If someone says, "I am hearing a train far away," they mean they can hear it right now. Ask yourself: is the word naming something you have, or something you are doing?
explain: A hearing can also be a meeting. «The court set a hearing for Monday.» Here a judge or a group listens to people before they decide something. Look at the words around it. Words like court, judge or decide are clues that you are in a meeting, not in your ears.
fact: Hearing is the sense that lets you notice sounds, using your ears.
fact: Hearing (verb) means noticing sounds right now: hear, hears, heard, hearing.
fact: A hearing is a meeting where a judge or a group listens to people before deciding something.
fact: «Hard of hearing» means someone has poor hearing, and a «hearing aid» helps them hear better.
fact: Long exposure to loud sound can damage hearing without any pain, and damaged hearing does not grow back, so protect your ears.
exercise: «To help someone with poor hearing, face them and speak clearly, without shouting.» What does hearing mean here? | *The sense that lets you notice sounds | Noticing a sound right now | A loud noise | A meeting where a judge listens to people
exercise: Which sentence uses hearing as a meeting? | Dogs have better hearing than people. | Loud music can damage your hearing. | *The court set a hearing for Monday morning. | I am hearing a bird singing outside.
exercise: «Long exposure to loud sound can damage hearing without any pain.» Which word in this sentence tells you that hearing is a thing you have? | loud | damage | without | *your
test: Jayden says, "I am hearing a train far away." What does hearing mean here? | A hearing aid | *Noticing a sound right now | The sense of touch | A meeting where a judge listens
test: Which phrase means someone has difficulty hearing? | within hearing | a hearing | hearing test | *hard of hearing
exam: In «a hearing test», hearing means: | *checking how well you can notice sounds with your ears | a loud noise that can damage your ears | the action of noticing a sound right now | a meeting where a judge listens to people
